  "notes": [
    "Chinese meals are shared: dishes go in the middle, and everyone takes from them.",
    "我请客 (wǒ qǐngkè) means \"my treat\". Friends often argue over who pays. Splitting is 分开付, or AA among young people.",
    "Call 服务员 (fúwùyuán) to get the waiter, and say 买单 (mǎidān) for the bill."
